<Base section="" title="Privacy · All Things Banana" description="How All Things Banana handles your data.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: 8 October 2026</em></p>
    <p>All Things Banana doesn't have accounts, doesn't set cookies and doesn't ask you for personal information.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Hosting:</strong> the site runs on Cloudflare, which processes basic request data (like your IP address) to deliver pages and protect against abuse.</li>
      <li><strong>Fonts:</strong> fonts load from Google Fonts, so your browser connects to Google's servers.</li>
      <li><strong>Links:</strong> feed items link to other websites, which have their own privacy policies.</li>
      <li><strong>Banana Cube:</strong> the puzzle runs entirely in your browser. Your moves aren't sent anywhere.</li>
      <li><strong>Banana popularity:</strong> each page you open adds one to that day's page-view total, which we show as a chart. That number is all we store: no IP address, cookie or identifier.</li>
      <li><strong>Banana Clicker:</strong> when you peel bananas, we add them to a total for the country your connection comes from, as reported by Cloudflare. We store only those country totals. Your own count is kept in your browser's local storage and never sent to us.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If we add advertising or analytics in the future, we'll update this page first and ask for consent where the law requires it.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
